    "warning": "A LIVE CAPTURE PROVES MORE THAN A HAND-BUILT SAMPLE, BUT IT IS STILL THE HAPPY PATH. This account is owned by the ACTING BANKER, and both endpoints scope reads to the caller. A banker reading a CUSTOMER's account behaves differently and asymmetrically: get_account returns 404 (loud - evidence missing, propose refuses) while list_account_transactions returns 200 with an EMPTY ARRAY (silent). The projection would then assert {accountId, count: 0, items: []} - 'this account has no transaction history' - when the truth is 'the banker cannot see them'. count: 0 is present and non-null, so EvidenceComplete PASSES and the approval record carries a false statement. This sample cannot detect that, and neither can the seam test. Deferred deliberately (Brian, 2026-09-08); named before `main`. It also does not prove the shape is stable - only that it was true at capture time."
